CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ declared outside: copied: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ declared inside: moved: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ nested block: moved: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ value of the exception object: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The exception object was a bitwise copy of the operand; it is now
initialized through the constructor that copy-initialization selects,
treating a move-eligible operand as an rvalue (try-block scopes are
recorded for [expr.prim.id.unqual]/15.3).
